####################################################################
# cat1b_withdraw.rq — CAT1b withdrawal condition. HAND-AUTHORED.
#
# Part of the answer to CQ8 (manuscript Table 1): which clinical alarms coincide with alarms
# carrying a technical condition that reduces the validity of that sensing
# pathway?
#
# A CAT1b flag ("asystole while an arterial line is present without alarms
# on its pathway") is withdrawn when an alarm on that same IBP pathway
# arrives while the flagged asystole is still active (agreed 2026-09-21),
# unless that alarm REASSURES (revised 2026-11-25, option A): its
# transducer is Arterial, it reports an increased arterial pressure or
# ScalingError, and nothing else (Enabled aside) — it then shows a working
# line delivering a pulsatile pressure, which supports the flag. A
# decreased pressure, out of range, a quality problem, a sensor fault or
# any venous/PA alarm withdraws. (Seen in the 40-patient sample: "ABP
# verkleinen" and "ABPm hoog" withdrew flags on artefactual asystoles.)
# The reason for withdrawing: in a genuine asystole the pressure alarm
# (a falling pressure, no pulse) naturally follows the ECG alarm
# by seconds, so the flag set at onset must not stand. The withdrawn
# asystole becomes evidence for a clinical event from this moment on.
#
# FLAGGED ALARMS (agreed 2026-11-25, all rules): an arriving IBP alarm that
# CAT1a has itself just flagged likely false positive withdraws nothing.
# (In practice the technical alarm behind its flag is on the same IBP unit,
# and that alarm's own arrival already withdrew the flag, or its presence
# blocked it.)
#
# A CAT1a flag rests on a signal or sensor, never on a functional unit, so a
# withdrawal never touches it. A stored flag lives in the flagged alarm's
# own transient graph, so only flags of alarms still active are found.
#
# CONTRACT. Bound on entry: ?new (the arriving alarm, on an IBP functional
# unit). Binds: ?flagged (the flagged alarm), ?fu, ?gFlag (the graph
# holding the flag).
# Used by actions/flag_withdraw_select.rq (logged as cat1b_withdrawn) and
# actions/flag_withdraw_delete.rq.
#
# VALIDATION — engine/regression.py: cat1b_withdraw and cat3a_withdraw
# (withdrawn), cat1b_borrow (forbidden firing: no withdrawal of the
# asystole there).
####################################################################

PREFIX mda:    <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>
PREFIX mdapoc: <https://w3id.org/mda/poc#>
PREFIX rdf:                   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs:                  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX owl:                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX physiologicalProperty: <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/physiological-property/>
PREFIX valuestate:            <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/metric-value-state/>
PREFIX qualitystate:          <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/quality-state/>
PREFIX opstate:               <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/operation-state/>
PREFIX position:              <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/anatomical-position/>

GRAPH ?gNew { ?new mda:hasMessage ?newMsg . ?newMsg mda:triggeredBy ?newDevice . }
FILTER NOT EXISTS { GRAPH ?gNew { ?new mdapoc:flaggedLikelyFalsePositive ?newFlagEvidence } }
BIND(IRI(CONCAT(STR(?new), "#persistent")) AS ?gNewP)
GRAPH ?gNewP { ?newDevice mda:hasFunctionalUnit ?fu . }
GRAPH ?gFlag { ?flagged mdapoc:flaggedLikelyFalsePositive ?fu }
# ... unless the arriving alarm REASSURES: it shows a working arterial line
# delivering a pulsatile pressure (same block as in cat1b_asystole_ibp.rq)
FILTER NOT EXISTS {
  GRAPH ?gNewP { ?fu mda:hasSensor ?okTransducer .
                 ?okTransducer mda:hasAnatomicalPosition position:Arterial . }
  { GRAPH ?gNew { ?okMetric mda:hasValueState ?okValue . }
    ?okValue mda:refinesConcept* valuestate:Increased .
    GRAPH ?gNewP { ?okMetric rdf:type ?okMetricType . }
    ?okMetricType rdfs:subClassOf* ?okRestriction .
    ?okRestriction owl:onProperty mda:approximates ;
                   owl:hasValue physiologicalProperty:ArterialPressure . }
  UNION
  { GRAPH ?gNew { ?okSignal mda:hasQualityState qualitystate:ScalingError . } }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    GRAPH ?gNew { ?anyNode ?anyStateProp ?anyState . }
    VALUES ?anyStateProp { mda:hasValueState mda:hasRhythm mda:hasQualityState
                           mda:hasSensorOperationState mda:hasComponentOperationState
                           mda:hasDeviceOperationState }
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?anyState mda:refinesConcept* valuestate:Increased }
    FILTER(?anyState NOT IN (qualitystate:ScalingError, opstate:Enabled))
  }
}
